From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Goossen <lucas.goossen@hey.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:09:40 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] media/gpu/v4l2: Leave room for the renderer in
 driver-allocated buffers

Without a frame pool (desktop Linux), V4L2VideoDecoder asks the driver
for num_codec_reference_frames + 2 CAPTURE buffers: the DPB, the frame
being decoded and one more. The renderer and the compositor hold decoded
frames too. After a seek in a paused <video>, the decoder refills its
DPB from the key frame while the renderer still holds frames. With a
1080p H.264 stream with B-frames (level 4.0, a DPB of 4, so 6 buffers)
the decoder runs out of buffers and the seek never completes; the same
stream labelled level 5.1 (a larger DPB, so more buffers) seeks fine.
Playback without seeking keeps going because the renderer releases
frames as it plays them.

Add limits::kMaxVideoFrames, the most frames the renderer queues, to the
driver-allocated count. The DMABUF path already asks for VIDEO_MAX_FRAME
shallow buffers and does not change.

AI-DISCLOSURE-PLACEHOLDER: replace with Lucas's own sentence.

Bug: TRACKING-BUG-PLACEHOLDER
Test: 1080p H.264 seeks with B-frames on Apple AVD: 8 of 8 done, 5 hung before
---
 media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_decoder.cc | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_decoder.cc b/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_decoder.cc
index 5ced27f6..4a0d5c7a 100644
--- a/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_decoder.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_decoder.cc
@@ -1204,10 +1204,13 @@ CroStatus V4L2VideoDecoder::ContinueChangeResolution(
   // If we don't use driver-allocated buffers, request as many as possible
   // (VIDEO_MAX_FRAME) since they are shallow allocations. Otherwise, allocate
   // |num_codec_reference_frames| plus one for the video frame being decoded,
-  // and one for our client (presumably an ImageProcessor).
-  const size_t v4l2_num_buffers = use_v4l2_allocated_buffers
-                                      ? num_codec_reference_frames + 2
-                                      : VIDEO_MAX_FRAME;
+  // one for our client (presumably an ImageProcessor), and the frames the
+  // renderer may hold. Without the last ones the decoder can run out of
+  // buffers while the renderer waits for a frame, e.g. after a seek.
+  const size_t v4l2_num_buffers =
+      use_v4l2_allocated_buffers
+          ? num_codec_reference_frames + 2 + limits::kMaxVideoFrames
+          : VIDEO_MAX_FRAME;
 
   VLOGF(1) << "Requesting: " << v4l2_num_buffers << " CAPTURE buffers of type "
            << (use_v4l2_allocated_buffers ? "V4L2_MEMORY_MMAP"
-- 
